Size the term label buffer in terms() for every separator, so a term
starting with the empty symbol no longer writes one byte past it.

Step 5 of termsform() in src/library/stats/src/model.c computed each
label's length adding one for the ':' separator only when the length so
far was positive, then filled a variable-length array of that size,
writing a ':' before every variable but the first.  The empty symbol has
a zero-length name, so a term starting with it, as in `(`(,) * g, got a
buffer one byte short and the terminating NUL landed past it (oss-fuzz
testcase 6138296798085120, formula target, through update.formula()).
Count each variable as its name plus one byte instead.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #527, R Bugzilla 19362 (both
2026-11-23).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/library/stats/src/model.c
+++ b/src/library/stats/src/model.c
@@ -2053,9 +2053,9 @@ SEXP termsform(SEXP args)
 #endif
 	for (int i = 1; i <= nvar; i++) {
 	    if (GetBit(CAR(call), i)) {
-		if (l > 0)
-		    l += 1;
-		l += (int) strlen(CHAR(STRING_ELT(varnames, i - 1)));
+		/* + 1 for the ':' before the next variable; not conditional
+		   on l > 0, as the empty symbol has a zero-length name */
+		l += strlen(CHAR(STRING_ELT(varnames, i - 1))) + 1;
 	    }
 	}
 #ifdef DEBUG_terms
